  "prefLabel": "Saf-C 6512.07 Denial of Certificate of Removal Hearing",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Saf-C 6512.07 Denial of Certificate of Removal Hearing.\n\n(a) A user who is denied a certificate of removal may request a hearing, pursuant to Saf-C 203.\n\n(b) The scope of the hearing shall be to determine if, by a preponderance of the evidence, whether:\n\n(1) The user has committed an interlock violation, as defined by RSA 265-A:38-a, I (a)-(i), within the preceding 120 days;\n\n(2) The expiration date of the ignition interlock order, including any extensions of time, has elapsed;\n\n(3) The user does not have any court or administrative hearings pending regarding an allegation of having committed one or more ignition interlock device violations; and\n\n(4) The user does not have any alleged ignition interlock program violations for which a hearing has yet to be scheduled.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note at chapter heading for Saf-C 6500) #13448, eff 9-20-22\n\nAPPENDIX A\n\nAPPENDIX B\n\nRule | Title | Obtain at:\n\nSaf-C 6501.03(a)(3) | Model Specifications for Breath Alcohol Ignition Interlock Devices (BAIIDs), National Highway Traffic Safety Administration, Volume 78, No. 89 of the Federal Register, Notice 26849, May 8, 2013 | Breath Alcohol Ignition Interlock Device (BAIID) Model Specifications.pdf (dot.gov)",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/saf-c6500.html"
}
